{"content_hash": "3e2fe01392476129", "version_id": 520, "article_id": 52, "level_code": "ja_n1", "lang": "ja", "level": 5, "level_label": "N1 上級", "title": "ドイツ銀行元トレーダー、金利操作で有罪判決取り消し", "title_zh": "德意志银行前交易员操纵利率定罪被推翻", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "bbc_business", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqgkvj10k6lno?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1620266757065-5814239881fd?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8ZGV1dHNjaGUlMjBiYW5rJTIwdHJhZGVyfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE2Nzc5NDl8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Kanchanara on Unsplash", "author": "Kanchanara", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@kanchanara?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/person-using-black-laptop-computer-5hcV51EeeWc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(271, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(309, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "14bf80248d84"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 306, "reading_minutes": 1.0, "lead": "金融危機後の金利操作スキャンダルで服役した元銀行員の有罪判決が、長年の法廷闘争を経て取り消された。英国控訴院は今週、バークレイズ元行員5人の判決も破棄しており、一連の冤罪が次々と覆りつつある。", "lead_zh": "金融危机后因操纵利率丑闻入狱的一名前银行职员，经过多年法律斗争，其有罪判决被推翻。英国上诉法院本周还撤销了五名巴克莱银行前员工的判决，一系列冤案正接连被平反。", "preview": "英国控訴院は、2018年に指標金利ユーリボルの「操作」で実刑判決を受けたドイツ銀行元トレーダー、クリスチャン・ビッタルの有罪判決を破棄した。ビッタル被告はビザが下りずスイスからビデオ回線で法廷を見守り、BBCに対し「この日を非常に長く待ち続けてきた」と語った。同じ控訴院は今週初め", "preview_zh": "英国上诉法院撤销了德意志银行前交易员克里斯蒂安·比特拉的有罪判决。他因2018年“操纵”基准利率欧元银行间同业拆借利率（Euribor）而入狱。比特拉因未获签证，只能在瑞士通过视频连线旁听庭审，他对BBC说：“这一天我等得太久了。”同一上诉法院本周早些时候还撤销了五名巴克莱银行前", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 508, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/52/ja_n1.mp3", "duration": 65.888, "size_bytes": 399024, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 197, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/520.json", "paragraphs": ["英国控訴院は、2018年に指標金利ユーリボルの「操作」で実刑判決を受けたドイツ銀行元トレーダー、クリスチャン・ビッタルの有罪判決を破棄した。ビッタル被告はビザが下りずスイスからビデオ回線で法廷を見守り、BBCに対し「この日を非常に長く待ち続けてきた」と語った。同じ控訴院は今週初め、金利操作裁判で有罪となったバークレイズ元行員5人の判決も取り消している。", "金融危機は2008年に始まり、世界に巨大な経済的衝撃を与え、多くの国で景気後退を引き起こした。銀行家への社会的反発が高まる一方、金融部門は納税者資金による救済で保護された。2012年には、危機勃発時に各行が貸出金利の設定過程で自らの立場を偽り、利益を膨らませ困難を隠していたことが発覚し、リボル・スキャンダルが噴出した。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["英国上诉法院撤销了德意志银行前交易员克里斯蒂安·比特拉的有罪判决。他因2018年“操纵”基准利率欧元银行间同业拆借利率（Euribor）而入狱。比特拉因未获签证，只能在瑞士通过视频连线旁听庭审，他对BBC说：“这一天我等得太久了。”同一上诉法院本周早些时候还撤销了五名巴克莱银行前员工在利率操纵案中的有罪判决。", "金融危机始于2008年，给全球带来巨大经济冲击，并在许多国家引发衰退。公众对银行家的反弹情绪高涨，而金融部门却靠纳税人出资的救助得到保护。2012年，人们发现银行在危机爆发时于贷款利率设定过程中谎报自身状况，借此抬高利润、掩盖困境，伦敦银行间同业拆借利率（Libor）丑闻由此爆发。"], "body": "英国控訴院は、2018年に指標金利ユーリボルの「操作」で実刑判決を受けたドイツ銀行元トレーダー、クリスチャン・ビッタルの有罪判決を破棄した。ビッタル被告はビザが下りずスイスからビデオ回線で法廷を見守り、BBCに対し「この日を非常に長く待ち続けてきた」と語った。同じ控訴院は今週初め、金利操作裁判で有罪となったバークレイズ元行員5人の判決も取り消している。\n\n金融危機は2008年に始まり、世界に巨大な経済的衝撃を与え、多くの国で景気後退を引き起こした。銀行家への社会的反発が高まる一方、金融部門は納税者資金による救済で保護された。2012年には、危機勃発時に各行が貸出金利の設定過程で自らの立場を偽り、利益を膨らませ困難を隠していたことが発覚し、リボル・スキャンダルが噴出した。", "body_zh": "英国上诉法院撤销了德意志银行前交易员克里斯蒂安·比特拉的有罪判决。他因2018年“操纵”基准利率欧元银行间同业拆借利率（Euribor）而入狱。比特拉因未获签证，只能在瑞士通过视频连线旁听庭审，他对BBC说：“这一天我等得太久了。”同一上诉法院本周早些时候还撤销了五名巴克莱银行前员工在利率操纵案中的有罪判决。\n\n金融危机始于2008年，给全球带来巨大经济冲击，并在许多国家引发衰退。公众对银行家的反弹情绪高涨，而金融部门却靠纳税人出资的救助得到保护。2012年，人们发现银行在危机爆发时于贷款利率设定过程中谎报自身状况，借此抬高利润、掩盖困境，伦敦银行间同业拆借利率（Libor）丑闻由此爆发。", "text": "英国控訴院は、2018年に指標金利ユーリボルの「操作」で実刑判決を受けたドイツ銀行元トレーダー、クリスチャン・ビッタルの有罪判決を破棄した。ビッタル被告はビザが下りずスイスからビデオ回線で法廷を見守り、BBCに対し「この日を非常に長く待ち続けてきた」と語った。同じ控訴院は今週初め、金利操作裁判で有罪となったバークレイズ元行員5人の判決も取り消している。 金融危機は2008年に始まり、世界に巨大な経済的衝撃を与え、多くの国で景気後退を引き起こした。銀行家への社会的反発が高まる一方、金融部門は納税者資金による救済で保護された。2012年には、危機勃発時に各行が貸出金利の設定過程で自らの立場を偽り、利益を膨らませ困難を隠していたことが発覚し、リボル・スキャンダルが噴出した。", "vocab": [{"word": "破棄", "pos": "noun", "zh": "撤销，废除", "note": "法律语境中常指判决被撤销", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "控訴院", "pos": "noun", "zh": "上诉法院", "note": "英国的上诉审法院", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "指標金利", "pos": "noun", "zh": "基准利率", "note": "金融报道常用词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "実刑判決", "pos": "noun", "zh": "实刑判决", "note": "指必须实际服刑的判决", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "有罪判決", "pos": "noun", "zh": "有罪判决", "note": "与無罪判決相对", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "取り消す", "pos": "verb", "zh": "取消，撤回", "note": "五段动词，此处为被动形", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "景気後退", "pos": "noun", "zh": "经济衰退", "note": "经济类文章高频词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "納税者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "纳税人", "note": "常与資金搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "救済", "pos": "noun", "zh": "救助，纾困", "note": "指政府出资救助企业", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "発覚", "pos": "noun", "zh": "被发现，败露", "note": "常与する连用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "内部告発者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "内部举报人", "note": "whistleblower 的译法", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "隠蔽", "pos": "noun", "zh": "隐瞒，掩盖", "note": "常含贬义", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "不正義", "pos": "noun", "zh": "不公，非正义", "note": "抽象名词，书面语", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "誤審", "pos": "noun", "zh": "误判", "note": "司法领域用词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "犠牲者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "牺牲者，受害者", "note": "此处指被当作替罪羊的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "スケープゴート", "pos": "noun", "zh": "替罪羊", "note": "外来语，政论文章常用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Ex-Deutsche Bank trader jailed for rigging rates has conviction overturned", "summary_original": "The Court of Appeal quashes the conviction of Christian Bittar, a former Deutsche Bank trader jailed in 2018.", "body_original": "Ex-Deutsche Bank trader jailed for rigging rates has conviction overturned\nBy\nAndy Verity\nFinancial investigations correspondent\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nAnother former banker sentenced in one of the biggest scandals of the financial crisis has had his conviction overturned following a long-running legal battle.\nThe Court of Appeal has quashed the conviction of Christian Bittar, a former Deutsche Bank trader who went to prison in 2018 for \"manipulating\" the benchmark interest rate, Euribor.\nIt comes after the same UK court overturned five convictions of ex-Barclays bankers in the rate rigging trials earlier this week.\nBittar, who watched proceedings via video link from Switzerland because he was not granted a visa to attend court, told the BBC: \"I have waited a very, very long time for this day.\"\nThe financial crisis began in 2008, sending huge economic shockwaves across the world and triggering recessions in many countries.\nThere was a public backlash against bankers, held by many to be responsible for the crisis, while the financial sector was protected by taxpayer-funded bailouts.\nThe Libor scandal erupted in 2012, when it was discovered that at the outbreak of the financial crisis, banks had been misrepresenting their positions during the process of setting the lending rate, helping to boost profits and mask difficulties.\nSome 19 City traders were convicted in the US and UK between 2015 and 2019 across nine criminal trials held in London and New York.\nEighteen of these have now been acquitted.\nOnly one former trader in the world now remains convicted: former Barclays trader Peter Johnson, who was also one of the original whistleblowers in the interest rate rigging scandal. He pleaded guilty on advice that he had little chance at winning at trial. The court confirmed that he too has now applied to appeal against his conviction.\nThe news has already prompted lawyers and senior politicians to press for the Bank of England and the Treasury to release all their records about their own roles in interest rate 'rigging' during the financial crisis, amid concerns raised of a cover-up of the role of central banks and governments.\n'Finally our injustice has been recognised'\nSpeaking after his conviction was quashed, Bittar said: \"Finally the injustice of what I and others suffered has been recognised.\n\"I am so grateful for those who stood by me through this ordeal and those who worked so tirelessly to correct it.\"\nHis wife, Caroline, who lives in the UK, said their family had lost 15 \"valuable years\", with their children \"growing up with this injustice\".\nShe added they were looking forward to \"enjoying life with our family and friends without this shadow hanging over us\".\nOn Wednesday, Jay Merchant, Jonathan Mathew, Alex Pabon, Colin Bermingham and Philippe Moryoussef saw their convictions for 'manipulating' the interest rate benchmarks Libor and Euribor quashed after a 10-year struggle for justice.\nThey launched fresh appeals against their jail sentences following a Supreme Court ruling last year that acquitted Tom Hayes, the first to be jailed for 'rigging' interest rates in 2015, and Carlo Palombo, jailed in 2019.\nTom Hayes, who was initially sentenced to 14 years, reduced on appeal to 11, is now seeking damages from his former employer UBS.\nThe traders were among 37 City traders and brokers prosecuted for \"manipulating\" the interest rate benchmarks Libor and Euribor, which track the cost of borrowing cash between the banks and have been used to set the interest rates on millions of mortgages and commercial loans.\nThe BBC has uncovered evidence of a much larger, state-led 'rigging' of interest rates, under pressure from central banks and governments across the world. Evidence implicating Downing Street and the Bank of England was suppressed throughout the criminal trials.\nFormer Conservative cabinet minister David Davis told the BBC the innocent traders had been the victims of a series of miscarriages of justice.\nHe said the people exonerated this week and before were \"the victims of a scapegoating exercise which arose as a result of the government's own misbehaviour in lowballing [falsely understating] Libor interest rates themselves, in order to try and rescue the economy after their own self-induced crash in the late 2000s\".\nIn 2015, during the first trial for interest rate 'rigging', of former UBS trader Hayes, Mr Justice Jeremy Cooke decided as a matter of law that any attempt to influence the rates could not be lawful, and that any rate influenced by commercial interest must automatically be false. Judges in the subsequent eight trials followed suit.\nHowever, in July 2025, the Supreme Court decided that all the judges had erred, misdirecting juries that it was wrong as a matter of law. Instead, whether the requests were right or wrong was properly a matter of fact for the jury to decide, not the judge.\nAll convictions in the United States were overturned in 2022 after an appeal court ruled that there was insufficient evidence that the traders' requests had broken any rules or laws.\nRelated topics\nUK Supreme Court\nDeutsche Bank\nBarclays\nSerious Fraud Office\nBanking\nMore on this story\nEx-bankers jailed for rigging rates have convictions quashed\nPublished\n3 days ago\nRate 'rigging' traders say they were scapegoated - now the Supreme Court will decide\nPublished\n26 May 2025", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:19:08.412879", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "英国", "s": 0.163, "e": 0.613, "sm": 162, "em": 612, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "控訴", "s": 0.625, "e": 0.963, "sm": 625, "em": 962, "cs": 2, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "院", "s": 0.975, "e": 1.188, "sm": 975, "em": 1187, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "は", "s": 1.2, "e": 1.425, "sm": 1200, "em": 1425, "cs": 5, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "、", "s": 1.425, "e": 1.75, "sm": 1425, "em": 1750, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "2018", "s": 1.75, "e": 2.62, "sm": 1750, "em": 2620, "cs": 7, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "年", "s": 2.62, "e": 2.837, "sm": 2620, "em": 2837, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "に", "s": 2.85, "e": 3.025, "sm": 2850, "em": 3025, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "指標", "s": 3.05, "e": 3.512, "sm": 3050, "em": 3512, "cs": 13, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "金利", "s": 3.525, "e": 3.9, "sm": 3525, "em": 3900, "cs": 15, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "ユーリボル